            <ArticleTitle>Subocclusion of the sinus node artery during coronary angioplasty: arrhythmological considerations.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>E35-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/clc.20638</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We report the case of a 58-year-old man who developed atrial fibrillation as a result of iatrogenic subocclusion of a diseased sinus node artery, originating from the left circumflex artery (LCx), occurring during LCx stenting, suggestive of an ischemic etiology of sinus node dysfunction.</AbstractText>
